From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 16:15:56 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/adreno: don't put the global address space at 2^48

adreno_iommu_create_vm() masked the vm base with GENMASK_ULL(48, 0).
That mask is 49 bits, so it keeps bit 48, and on msm8998 -- where the
GPU SMMU hands out a TTBR1 aperture of
0xffff000000000000-0xffffffffffffffff -- it produced a base of
exactly 2^48.

2^48 is in neither half of a split address space. The hardware
translates 48-bit VAs, so TTBR0 covers 0..2^48-1 and TTBR1 covers
0xffff000000000000 and up. Everything the kernel puts in this vm --
ringbuffers, memptrs, the rptr shadow, preemption records -- therefore
landed at an address the GPU could not reach. It truncated those VAs
to 48 bits, so a buffer at 2^48 + X was accessed as X, looked up in
TTBR0 where nothing maps it, and faulted on a write.

Measured on taimen (originally against the pre-drm_gpuvm
adreno_iommu_create_address_space() this function has since become).
A 1 MB buffer allocated at 2^48+0x78000 masks to 0x78000 and spans
0x78000..0x178000; the fault two milliseconds later was a write to
0xb8000, inside it. The SMMU fault registers agree: far=0xb8000 with a
non-zero ttbr0, cbfrsynra=0 (the GPU's stream id) and FSYNR0.WNR set.

The base was masked because this aperture ends at U64_MAX and
start + size is then 2^64, which wraps to zero and leaves drm_mm with
a broken range -- every allocation fails and msm_gpu_init() dies with
"could not allocate memptrs: -28", taking the display down with it.
Clamping the size keeps the range representable while leaving the
base in the half the hardware expects, so the allocations come back
as 0xffff000000000000, 0xffff000000003000 and so on.

Beyond removing the faults this is the difference between a
recoverable stall and a dead phone: with the vm at 2^48, opening a
GL-heavy application reset the SoC outright -- no oops, no panic, no
console output -- and burned the bootloader's slot retries until it
fell back to fastboot. With the base corrected the device stays up.

Ported from taimen-v6.0 onto 6.18, where
adreno_iommu_create_address_space() has been renamed
adreno_iommu_create_vm() and returns struct drm_gpuvm * via
msm_gem_vm_create() instead of struct msm_gem_address_space * via
msm_gem_address_space_create(); the fix itself carries over unchanged.

Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/adreno_gpu.c | 30 +++++++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 28 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/adreno_gpu.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/adreno_gpu.c
index 4b5a4edd0702..61f67eef3682 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/adreno_gpu.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/adreno_gpu.c
@@ -217,8 +217,34 @@ adreno_iommu_create_vm(struct msm_gpu *gpu,
 	start = max_t(u64, SZ_16M, geometry->aperture_start);
 	size = geometry->aperture_end - start + 1;
 
-	vm = msm_gem_vm_create(gpu->dev, mmu, "gpu", start & GENMASK_ULL(48, 0),
-			       size, true);
+	/*
+	 * Use the aperture base as it is, and clamp the size instead of masking
+	 * the base into GENMASK_ULL(48, 0).
+	 *
+	 * That mask is 49 bits, so it keeps bit 48. Measured on msm8998, whose
+	 * GPU SMMU reports a TTBR1 aperture of
+	 * 0xffff000000000000-0xffffffffffffffff, it produced a base of exactly
+	 * 2^48 -- an address in neither half of the split address space, since
+	 * the hardware translates 48-bit VAs (TTBR0 0..2^48-1, TTBR1
+	 * 0xffff000000000000 and up). The GPU then truncated those VAs to 48
+	 * bits, so a global buffer at 2^48 + X was accessed as X, looked up in
+	 * TTBR0 where nothing maps it, and faulted on a write.
+	 *
+	 * The reason the base was masked at all is that this aperture ends at
+	 * U64_MAX: start + size is 2^64, which wraps to 0 and leaves drm_mm with
+	 * a broken range, so every allocation fails and msm_gpu_init() dies with
+	 * "could not allocate memptrs: -28". Clamping the size keeps the range
+	 * representable while leaving the base in the half the hardware expects.
+	 */
+	if (start + size < start)
+		size = U64_MAX - start;
+
+	DRM_DEV_INFO(&pdev->dev,
+		     "gpu aspace: aperture %#llx-%#llx, base %#llx, size %#llx\n",
+		     geometry->aperture_start, geometry->aperture_end,
+		     start, size);
+
+	vm = msm_gem_vm_create(gpu->dev, mmu, "gpu", start, size, true);
 
 	if (IS_ERR(vm) && !IS_ERR(mmu))
 		mmu->funcs->destroy(mmu);
